<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm4b-jiuquan ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 4B / Yaogan 53-07..09 + 56-19..21 (Jiuquan) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 22.5 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 1.715 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.5621-0.001428*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: Long March 4B (sim/vehicles/lm4b.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-4B: Wikipedia infobox stage data; S1 shutdown 153.06 s / S3 shutdown 648.68 s (huijiwiki, Yaogan-51 flight) used as checks; dry masses ASSUMED.
Flown: LL2 Success 19:25Z. Az 109 from debris-zone notice/NOTAMs. Published check: S3 shutdown 648.68 s on Yaogan-51 flight (huijiwiki).
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 109.00 deg; payload 2000 kg.
Pad: 40.960482N 100.298059E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-23T19:25:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
